From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:40:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] driver_cmd_fallback: answer MACADDR from the network interface

The generic fallback returns an empty reply for MACADDR. The AIDL
supplicant interface rejects it, and Android's PMK cache cannot identify
the interface. Use the existing Linux ioctl helper to obtain the actual
current interface address and return the format expected by the AIDL
implementation. Propagate ioctl and reply-truncation failures.

The board must select lib_driver_cmd_fallback as its
BOARD_WPA_SUPPLICANT_PRIVATE_LIB; otherwise ANDROID_LIB_STUB removes the
nl80211 driver-command callback and this implementation is never reached.

Use the fully qualified Soong dependency
//external/wpa_supplicant_8/wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant:lib_driver_cmd_fallback
in BoardConfig.mk. Exporting that namespace also exposes Cuttlefish
wpa_supplicant and hostapd modules with duplicate names.

Other Android-private driver commands retain their existing behavior;
this does not claim support for vendor coexistence or suspend commands.

Origin: Local ThinkSmart View port
Source: https://github.com/LineageOS/android_external_wpa_supplicant_8
License: Apache-2.0 (modified upstream sources)
Base-commit: 1063d796b547c4cd2c23c21da72ed988ac70a84a
Apply in filename order within this project.

---
diff --git a/wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant/libdrivercmdfallback/driver_cmd_nl80211.c b/wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant/libdrivercmdfallback/driver_cmd_nl80211.c
index 6cdc57a..510fbd8 100644
--- a/wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant/libdrivercmdfallback/driver_cmd_nl80211.c
+++ b/wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant/libdrivercmdfallback/driver_cmd_nl80211.c
@@ -20,9 +20,25 @@
 #include "includes.h"
 
 #include "common.h"
+#include "driver_nl80211.h"
+#include "linux_ioctl.h"
 
 int wpa_driver_nl80211_driver_cmd(void* priv, char* cmd, char* buf,
                                   size_t buf_len) {
+  if (os_strcasecmp(cmd, "MACADDR") == 0) {
+    struct i802_bss* bss = priv;
+    u8 addr[ETH_ALEN];
+    int ret;
+
+    if (linux_get_ifhwaddr(bss->drv->global->ioctl_sock, bss->ifname, addr))
+      return -1;
+    ret = os_snprintf(buf, buf_len, "Macaddr = " MACSTR "\n", MAC2STR(addr));
+    if (os_snprintf_error(buf_len, ret)) {
+      wpa_printf(MSG_ERROR, "MACADDR reply buffer is too small");
+      return -1;
+    }
+    return ret;
+  }
   return 0;
 }
 
